/* QubeC grammar: the source of truth for the lexical and syntactic grammar.
 *
 * Notation: the EBNF of XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition), section 6, without its [ wfc: ] and
 * [ vc: ] annotations (spec section 1.3.6). [D0078]
 *   - A difference A - B that is one item of a longer sequence is written in parentheses.
 *   - The operator - appears only in lexical productions, and its right operand matches
 *     only finitely many strings.
 *
 * Layers: [D0079]
 *   - Section 1, the lexical grammar: names in UPPER_SNAKE_CASE, matching characters, with
 *     nothing implicit between parts. TOKEN lists the kinds of token, TRIVIA the kinds of
 *     trivia; every other lexical production is a helper production.
 *   - Section 2, the syntactic grammar: names in UpperCamelCase, matching tokens, with trivia
 *     allowed between any two tokens. The start symbol is SourceFile. A quoted string denotes
 *     exactly one token. No helper production is referred to.
 *
 * Each production cites the decisions it implements in a trailing comment: [Dnnnn].
 * The specification quotes productions from this file verbatim.
 * Checked by tools/grammar/ (D0080, D0081).
 */

/* ===== Section 1: lexical grammar =====
 *
 * No productions yet (T0015-T0019).
 */

/* ===== Section 2: syntactic grammar =====
 *
 * No productions yet (M03 writes SourceFile).
 */
